
| Property                                 | Sliding Window   | Prefix Sum + HashMap |
| ---------------------------------------- | ---------------- | -------------------- |
| Monotonic constraint                     | ✅ required       | ❌ not needed         |
| Handles negative numbers                 | ❌ usually breaks | ✅                    |
| Handles equality (`==`)                  | ❌                | ✅                    |
| Find longest / count with `≤ k` or `≥ k` | ✅                | ❌                    |
| Find longest / count with `== k`         | ❌                | ✅                    |
| At most K type constraints               | ✅                | ❌                    |
| Exactly K type constraints               | ❌                | ✅                    |

When you see a subarray problem, ask: Does expanding the window move the condition in only one direction?

If YES → sliding window
If NO → prefix sum

Step 1:
-------
Are all numbers non-negative?
    If NO → sliding window probably fails → use prefix sums.
    If YES → go to Step 2.

Step 2:
-------
Is the condition:
    ≤ k
    ≥ k
    at most k
    at least k
→ sliding window.

If the condition is:
    == k
    exactly k
    balanced
    equal counts
→ prefix sum.

